#: ../../../xonsh_session.rst:294
msgid "All of these forms accept the same ``cmds`` shape:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xonsh_session.rst:296
msgid ""
"``cmds`` is a list of \"commands\", each command being a list of argument "
"strings/tuples."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xonsh_session.rst:298
msgid "Multiple commands separated by ``\"|\"`` form a pipe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xonsh_session.rst:299
msgid "A trailing ``\"&\"`` runs the pipeline in the background."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xonsh_session.rst:301
msgid ""
"So ``$(ls -la | grep .py)`` becomes ``subproc_captured_stdout(['ls', '-la'], "
"'|', ['grep', '.py'])``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xonsh_session.rst:304
msgid ""
"This is exactly what the :class:`xonsh.built_ins.Cmd` builder produces, "
"which is why you can write the same pipeline two ways:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xonsh_session.rst:307
msgid ""
"# As literal subprocess sugar\n"
"out = $(git log --oneline -5 | head -3)\n"
"\n"
"# Or built explicitly via the Cmd helper\n"
"out = (\n"
"    @.imp.xonsh.built_ins\n"
"    .Cmd(__xonsh__, 'git', 'log', '--oneline', '-5')\n"
"    .pipe('head', '-3')\n"
"    .out()    # dispatches to subproc_captured_stdout\n"
")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xonsh_session.rst:320
msgid "Other dispatch helpers on the builder map 1:1 to the table above:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xonsh_session.rst:322
msgid "``Cmd.out()``  → ``$()``  (``subproc_captured_stdout``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xonsh_session.rst:323
msgid "``Cmd.run()``  → ``$[]``  (``subproc_uncaptured``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xonsh_session.rst:324
msgid "``Cmd.obj()``  → ``!()``  (``subproc_captured_object``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xonsh_session.rst:325
msgid "``Cmd.hide()`` → ``![]``  (``subproc_captured_hiddenobject``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xonsh_session.rst:327
msgid ""
"Use the literal forms in interactive code, and the dispatcher / builder API "
"when the command list is **dynamic** — for example built from user input, "
"generated in a loop, or driven by config."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xonsh_session.rst:332
msgid "Other AST-invoked helpers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xonsh_session.rst:334
msgid ""
"A few more attributes on ``__xonsh__`` exist because xonsh's parser rewrites "
"special syntax into calls on them. You normally do not call these directly, "
"but it is useful to know they are there:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xonsh_session.rst:338
msgid ""
"``pathsearch`` / ``globsearch`` / ``regexsearch`` / ``regexmatchsearch`` — "
"implement backtick expressions (```regex```, ``g`glob```, etc.) and ``$VAR`` "
"glob expansion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xonsh_session.rst:341
msgid "``glob`` — wrapper used by glob expansion in subproc mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xonsh_session.rst:342
msgid "``expand_path`` — applied to bare path arguments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xonsh_session.rst:343
msgid ""
"``call_macro`` / ``enter_macro`` — power xonsh **macro** calls (``f!(...)``) "
"and macro context managers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xonsh_session.rst:345
msgid "``path_literal`` — backs the ``p\"...\"`` Path literal syntax."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xonsh_session.rst:346
msgid ""
"``help`` / ``superhelp`` — back ``obj?`` and ``obj??`` for Python objects "
"(the subproc-mode counterparts live in ``xonsh.procs.specs`` and ``xonsh."
"aliases.print_alias_help``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xonsh_session.rst:349
msgid "``eval_fstring_field`` — backs xonsh's f-string field evaluation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xonsh_session.rst:350
msgid ""
"``list_of_strs_or_callables`` / ``list_of_list_of_strs_outer_product`` — "
"flatten the heterogeneous argument lists xonsh's parser produces before "
"dispatching to subproc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xonsh_session.rst:355
msgid ""
"When in doubt, prefer ``@.<x>`` (``XSH.interface``) for the four stable bits "
"of the API, and treat everything on ``__xonsh__`` as power-user territory "
"that should be guarded with try/except and feature checks."
msgstr ""

